# Cloud Run entrypoint.
#
# Without this file the buildpack starts gunicorn with its default 30 second
# worker timeout, and a fine resolution heatmap gets killed mid calculation
# with [CRITICAL] WORKER TIMEOUT. The browser then sees a 500.
#
# --timeout 0 is what Google recommends for Cloud Run. Cloud Run enforces its
# own request timeout, so gunicorn does not need a second one.
#
# --threads 1 keeps one request per instance. A fine grid peaks near 320 MB and
# an instance gets 512 MiB, so two at once would not fit. Cloud Run starts
# another instance instead, which is what you want.
web: gunicorn --bind :$PORT --workers 1 --threads 1 --timeout 0 app:app
